menu "espOS BLE gateway"

    config ESPOS_BLE_POST_BATCH_MAX
        int "Advertisements per POST"
        default 40
        range 1 200
        help
            How many buffered advertisements one POST to
            /signalk/v2/api/ble/gateway/advertisements carries. Bounded so a
            flush in a busy marina cannot build an unbounded JSON document;
            what does not fit waits for the next ble.post_int_ms. The batch
            scratch is a static array (about 128 bytes per slot) and the
            serialised JSON is built on the heap, so raising this costs RAM
            twice over.

    config ESPOS_BLE_WS_BUFFER
        int "Control WebSocket frame buffer (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 1024 16384
        help
            esp_websocket_client's buffer for the control socket. A
            gatt_subscribe for a device with many characteristics and init
            writes has to arrive in one frame -- the 1 KiB buffer of the
            implementation this replaced could not reassemble it. It also
            bounds the status frames going the other way.

    config ESPOS_BLE_GATTC_MAX_CONN
        int "Simultaneous GATT connections"
        default 3
        range 1 7
        help
            Connection slots in the GATT client and in the gateway's session
            table. The runtime setting ble.max_gatt_sess is clamped to this
            and its descriptor (config/ble.json) also says 3, so raise both.
            Bluedroid must be built for at least this many ACL links
            (BT_ACL_CONNECTIONS); on the ESP32-P4 the C6 co-processor's
            controller sets the real ceiling.

    config ESPOS_BLE_STACK_SIZE
        int "Gateway task stack size (bytes)"
        default 8192
        range 4096 32768
        help
            The task that serialises batches with cJSON and POSTs them
            through esp_http_client. The big scratch buffers are static, so
            this covers call depth, not payloads; a stack-protection fault
            here is a reboot loop rather than a degraded mode, hence the
            headroom.

    config ESPOS_BLE_STACK_IN_PSRAM
        bool "Put the gateway task's stack in PSRAM"
        depends on SPIRAM && FREERTOS_TASK_CREATE_ALLOW_EXT_MEM
        default y
        help
            The gateway task never touches flash, so its stack may live in
            PSRAM, which frees ESPOS_BLE_STACK_SIZE bytes of internal RAM. That
            matters on a single-chip board such as the ESP32-C5, where BLE,
            WiFi and the SignalK client share ~170 KB of internal RAM.

endmenu
